1
00:00:01,459 --> 00:00:04,863
Meet MADHAV Order Desk: a simple way for small bakeries

2
00:00:04,863 --> 00:00:08,266
to turn customer messages into checked orders, with the owner

3
00:00:08,266 --> 00:00:08,947
in control.

4
00:00:10,132 --> 00:00:14,360
Aanya asks in Hinglish for one chocolate cake tomorrow. Let's

5
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,628
prepare the reply.

6
00:00:16,815 --> 00:00:21,010
The sample parser identifies her product, quantity and pickup date

7
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:25,205
for owner review. AMD live analysis is separately implemented, but

8
00:00:25,205 --> 00:00:26,463
not shown here.

9
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:31,338
The catalog—not the AI—sets the price at nine hundred rupees,

10
00:00:31,338 --> 00:00:34,680
with a suggested four hundred and fifty rupee advance.

11
00:00:35,866 --> 00:00:40,086
Only my approval reserves the cake. Preparing the draft never

12
00:00:40,086 --> 00:00:40,930
books it.

13
00:00:42,118 --> 00:00:45,651
I approve the reply separately. Here it appears in the

14
00:00:45,651 --> 00:00:48,478
demo chat; it's not a real WhatsApp send.

15
00:00:49,664 --> 00:00:53,520
The order book now shows Aanya's nine hundred rupee order.

16
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:55,448
No payment has been recorded.

17
00:00:56,667 --> 00:01:00,490
Rohan wants Red Velvet. Let's check what happens when a

18
00:01:00,490 --> 00:01:02,019
product is sold out.

19
00:01:03,208 --> 00:01:08,234
Capacity is zero. MADHAV blocks the booking and offers available

20
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:11,752
alternatives. It never substitutes a product automatically.

21
00:01:13,466 --> 00:01:17,717
Rohan chooses vanilla in a follow-up. The new customer message

22
00:01:17,717 --> 00:01:19,418
is fictional demo data.

23
00:01:20,604 --> 00:01:24,352
We review the new proposal: one vanilla cake, seven hundred

24
00:01:24,352 --> 00:01:25,476
and fifty rupees.

25
00:01:26,708 --> 00:01:31,028
Now I approve the vanilla order and its reply. Red

26
00:01:31,028 --> 00:01:32,324
Velvet remains unbooked.

27
00:01:33,494 --> 00:01:36,494
Meera needs two cupcake boxes tomorrow.

28
00:01:37,690 --> 00:01:41,008
The catalog price is four hundred and twenty per box.

29
00:01:41,008 --> 00:01:43,330
That's eight hundred and forty in total.

30
00:01:44,550 --> 00:01:48,198
I reserve this order and approve the confirmation separately.

31
00:01:49,379 --> 00:01:52,333
In Orders, we can see the full eight hundred and

32
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:53,219
forty rupee total.

33
00:01:54,877 --> 00:01:59,271
Now I manually record four hundred and twenty rupees received,

34
00:01:59,271 --> 00:02:00,589
after independent confirmation.

35
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:05,380
MADHAV shows four hundred and twenty paid, and four hundred

36
00:02:05,380 --> 00:02:09,012
and twenty still due. A payment claim never changes the

37
00:02:09,012 --> 00:02:09,739
ledger automatically.

38
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:16,030
AMD handles language understanding. Our code enforces prices, stock and

39
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:21,150
owner approval. This is a chat simulation; official WhatsApp integration

40
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:23,198
comes later. That's MADHAV.

